- [ ] Screen reachable by authorized operator (verified by logging in and navigating)
- [ ] Deep-link from alerts/incidents works (direct URL navigation without sidebar click)

### Action Wiring

- [ ] Action wiring verified end-to-end (UI action → API call → persisted result)
- [ ] All CRUD operations that exist in the API are accessible from the UI (or explicitly marked backend-only)
- [ ] Workflow transitions exposed in the UI match the backend lifecycle rules

### Access Control

- [ ] Permission-denied behavior verified (403 returned from API, action disabled/hidden in UI)
- [ ] RBAC gate documented in visibility matrix
- [ ] `require_permission()` present on all backend endpoints for this route
- [ ] Frontend `can()` gates present for cross-domain calls and destructive actions
- [ ] Tenant-boundary negative verified for route data and mutations where applicable

### UI States

- [ ] Loading state shown while data fetches
- [ ] Empty state shown when no data exists
- [ ] Error state shown on API failure (toast or inline error)
- [ ] Validation and conflict errors surfaced clearly to the operator
- [ ] Destructive, archive, or approval actions require deliberate confirmation where appropriate

### Data Integrity & Workflow Controls

- [ ] Invalid workflow transitions are blocked in the UI and backend
- [ ] Required fields and domain invariants are enforced consistently
- [ ] Server truth is not reconstructed in the client through unsafe fan-out or hidden assumptions

### Performance & Scale

- [ ] Route avoids N+1 or client fan-out patterns for normal operator usage
- [ ] Search, filtering, sorting, and pagination are server-side where volume warrants it
- [ ] Route remains usable with realistic tenant data volume

### Audit & Observability

- [ ] Audit trail present for user-initiated actions (`log_audit_event()` / `log_user_action()` — per-repo helper name varies)
- [ ] Toast notifications shown on mutation success/failure
- [ ] Operator-visible errors are truthful and actionable
- [ ] Logs or traces provide enough context to debug failed actions

